# Arena Liferay Portal 7.4.3.129-ga129-specific Aikido scan excludes.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# EXCLUDE SEMANTICS — measured against local-scanner v1.0.139 on 2026-08-29
# (synthetic-repo probe; see KnowledgeBase docs/security/aikido-security-scanning.md).
# `--exclude` is a plain SUBSTRING match on the candidate path. NOT a glob.
#   * any pattern containing `*` is INERT and fails silently: `**/build/**`,
#     `build/**` and `bin/**` match nothing, and the scan runs at full scope.
#     Every pattern in this file before 2026-08-29 was of that form, i.e. the
#     entire file was a no-op.
#   * a bare word matches anywhere inside a path, including inside a longer
#     name (`uild` excludes `build/`), so always slash-wrap: `/build/`.
#   * there is NO root anchoring. `/bin/` also hits nested bin dirs.
#   * the secrets stage (gitleaks) ignores --exclude completely and walks
#     everything; only pre-scan cleanup or --scan-types affects its cost.
# The local wrapper warns about inert patterns before every scan.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# One pattern per line (# comments allowed), passed as --exclude by BOTH
# scan consumers - keep them in parity when tuning scope or timeouts:
#   local: ~/.agents/manual-skills/aikido-scan/scripts/aikido-scan.sh
#   CI:    .github/workflows/aikido.yml (manual dispatch)
# Kept here (repo root) rather than inside either consumer so the skill
# stays portable to other projects unmodified and CI picks up the same list.

# IDE-generated build/compiled-class output for the Ant-built core modules.
# Verified via `git ls-files | grep -E "(^|/)build/"` - zero tracked files
# live under any build/ directory anywhere in this repo, so matching every
# depth is safe.
/build/

# Stray JVM heap dump left in the working tree (modules/apps/foundation/
# portal/java_pid83209.hprof). May contain sensitive memory contents and has
# no reason to exist in the working tree - consider deleting it directly.
.hprof

# Test/integration-test source inside otherwise-in-scope production modules.
# Segment-precise, so main sources are untouched.
/src/test/
/src/testIntegration/

# Integration-test helper MODULES under modules/** (552 dirs, ~1.9k tracked
# files). Their sources sit in their own src/main/java, so the src/test
# excludes above never reach them. `<artifact>-test` and `-test-util` bundles
# exist only to run tests inside a live portal and ship in no release dist.
#
# NEVER write these as `-test/` / `-test-util/`. A pattern starting with a
# hyphen is forwarded verbatim into checkov's `--skip-path` and Semgrep's
# argv, where argparse reads it as a flag: the IaC scan dies with
# "argument --skip-path: expected one argument" and the SAST scan with
# "failed to output result". Both types then produce NO findings while the
# run still exits 0 - two silently dead scanners. Measured 2026-08-29 on
# v1.0.139; the scan wrapper now refuses such patterns.
#
# The hyphen-free forms below cover the same modules (substring match, so
# "test/" is contained in "<artifact>-test/"). Safe in THIS repo because it
# holds no `latest/` path (verified: `git ls-files | grep -c latest/` = 0) -
# recheck that before copying these two lines to another repo, since
# "latest/" contains "test/".
test/
test-util/

# Local npm tarball cache under modules/ (untracked @pkg-version.tgz files,
# reproducible from yarn.lock). Untracked, so CI checkouts never contain it.
/modules/node_modules_cache/

# Whole test-only module tree. Parent-qualified so only this path matches,
# never other `test` dirs.
/modules/test/

# Release-engineering metadata mirror: artifact/app .properties, .changelog
# and icons recording upstream coordinates. None of it is built or shipped.
/modules/.releng/

# Upstream DXP-only sources, mirrored for upgrade parity but never built or
# deployed by this CE fork. Verified against the release bundle: no leaf
# project under modules/dxp/** matches any of the 1434 shipped jars.
/modules/dxp/

# Docs-only and non-production ROOT trees whose name occurs nowhere nested
# (verified 2026-08-29 with `git ls-files | grep -E "/<name>/"` = 0 hits), so
# the un-anchorable substring form is exact here.
/learn-resources/
/portal-test/
/oss-licenses/
/nbproject/
/readme/
/build-test-batch/

# NOTE: node_modules is intentionally NOT excluded. Aikido's JS supply-chain
# coverage is real scanning surface, not noise - a security-coverage decision,
# not cleanup. Discuss before adding it.
# NOTE: "scripts" and "tools" are deliberately NOT excluded: scripts/ holds
# this branch's release tooling and tools/ holds dev/release shell scripts -
# both stay in scope as secret-scan surface.
#
# UNRESOLVED - root-only trees that CANNOT be expressed under substring
# semantics. Each was root-anchored on purpose in the pre-2026-08-29 file to
# avoid hitting same-named dirs under production modules, and there is no way
# to anchor now. Tracked-file counts measured 2026-08-29 as root/nested:
